#: src/panels.tsx
msgid "panels.method.parityTerm"
msgstr "Parity capacity"

#: src/panels.tsx
msgid "panels.method.parityBody"
msgstr "is calculated by this page from each array's configured disk count and RAID level. It cannot be calculated while an array is not assembled, and then reads \"Not measurable\". A member marked faulty does not change how many disks the array occupies, so this figure does not move either; faulty and spare markers show up only in the member list and the state badge. Being calculated, it can differ very slightly from the real size."

#: src/panels.tsx
msgid "panels.method.usedBody"
msgstr "is measured directly on the mounted filesystem. If it is not mounted, or the query fails, this is left as \"Not measurable\" rather than estimated."

#: src/panels.tsx
msgid "panels.method.rawBody"
msgstr "includes the system disk the OS is installed on, but that disk is excluded from RAID candidates and so does not appear in unallocated physical capacity."

